Q. S3 Bucket Policies?
A:	S3 Bucket Policies are JSON-based access control rules that define who can access your bucket and what actions they can perform.
They are applied at the bucket level and control access for all objects inside the bucket.
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow" | "Deny",
      "Principal": "* or AWS Account/ARN",
      "Action": "s3:ActionName",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name[/object-key]"
    }
  ]
}


🔹 Fields Meaning:
Version → Policy language version (always "2012-10-17" for new policies).
Statement → One or more permission rules.
Effect → "Allow" or "Deny".
Principal → Who gets the permission (* for everyone, or specific AWS account/ARN).
Action → S3 operation (e.g., s3:GetObject, s3:PutObject).
Resource → ARN of bucket or object(s).

